# stray root-level Verilog from elaboration tests that don't set a target dir
/*.v
unnamed.v
# Vivado / synthesis artifacts (keep scripts in synth/, ignore outputs)
synth/*.rpt
synth/*.log
synth/*.jou
synth/*.dcp
# Raw Vivado transcripts from synth/run_walker_dcache_gate.sh. The distilled
# `*.summary` beside each one IS committed -- that is the gate evidence.
synth/*.out
# Archived gate evidence keeps only its distilled *.summary. The raw Vivado .rpt/.out
# per-arm reports were stripped from history 2026-09-12: they are bulky, regenerable
# from the pinned netlist md5 recorded alongside each result, and are not the record
# anyone reads. Checkpoints were never tracked at all -- a synth+routed DCP pair is
# ~85 MB per arm.
synth/archive/**/*.dcp
synth/fullcore_synth.md5
# Generated by impl_FullCore.tcl when IMPL_PROBE_PERIOD_NS is set. The committed
# constraint is synth/clk.xdc (5.000ns); this file is a transient measurement artifact
# and must never be mistaken for the spec.
synth/clk_probe.xdc
# Router byproduct dropped in the CWD; impl_FullCore.tcl copies the useful content to
# synth/fullcore_congested_nets.txt, which is itself a regenerable report.
iter_100_CongestedCLBsAndNets.txt
synth/fullcore_congested_nets.txt
clockInfo.txt
.Xil/
vivado*.log
vivado*.jou
cong/
synth/vivado_*.log
bench_logs/

# --- 2026-09-05 audit: ~38 MB of derived artifacts were sitting untracked ---
# Python bytecode from tools/
__pycache__/
# Vivado stdout transcripts. Same rule as synth/*.out above: the distilled
# *.summary beside them is the committed evidence, the raw transcript is not.
synth/*.stdout
# Pinned/archived build products and gate scratch dirs -- large and regenerable
# from the netlist md5 recorded alongside each gate result.
synth/pinned/
synth/fpucore_gate/
# Fuzz and ported-test run logs. The triage conclusions are written up in
# docs/superpowers/specs/; these are the raw per-seed transcripts behind them.
fuzz_logs*/
ported_logs_*/
# ROM disassembly -- 13 MB, regenerable from files/*.rom
*.dis

# Vivado design checkpoints are build artifacts and must NEVER be tracked.
# ~675 MB of history was once consumed by eleven ~59 MB fullcore_routed.dcp files
# under exp4ns/ exp5ns/ exp5ns_implonly/ -- paths the earlier synth/*.dcp rules did
# not cover. Stripped from history 2026-09-12; these patterns stop a recurrence.
*.dcp
exp*/**/*.dcp

# --- 2026-09-12 pre-publication sweep ---
# Build/run artifacts are never tracked, at any depth. Earlier rules were anchored to
# synth/ only, so ~135 report+transcript files and 120 agent/fuzz logs had accumulated
# under archive/, probe_*/ and the repo root. All stripped from history; these patterns
# are what stop a recurrence. The durable evidence is the distilled *.summary files and
# the write-ups in docs/ -- not the raw tool output behind them.
*.log
*.jou
*.rpt
*.out
*.stdout
*.STOPPED.md
# Agent-framework task reports: development process state, not project documentation.
.superpowers/
/tools/musashi/.build/
/tools/musashi/*.o
/tools/musashi/*.a
/tools/musashi/musashi_run
